// ============================================================================
// 51-eclipse-service-control.rules
//
// PolicyKit rule granting user 'mcornelison' the
// org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage-units action, SCOPED to a fixed allow-list of
// eclipse-* units + verbs. This is the A-7 privilege path for the US-403 System
// Setup menu: the chromium dashboard kiosk runs UNPRIVILEGED and asks the local
// state server to run `systemctl <verb> <unit>`; this rule is what authorizes
// those calls without sudo/root.
//
// Why a SIBLING 51- file (not a widening of 50-eclipse-obd-poweroff.rules): that
// rule grants ONLY org.freedesktop.login1.power-off and explicitly says new
// privileges get a new file. This rule is a different action entirely
// (manage-units), so it lives on its own (50- comment: "add a SECOND rule file
// (51-...) rather than widening this one").
//
// Allow-list (mirrors src/pi/splash/service_control.py SERVICE_ALLOWLIST):
//   eclipse-obd.service        -> start / stop / restart   (data capture)
//   eclipse-sync.service       -> start / stop / restart   (server upload)
//   eclipse-dashboard.service  -> stop / restart           (A-8 Exit = stop kiosk)
//   eclipse-powerwatch.service -> restart ONLY             (D-7 safe-shutdown guard)
//
// SAFETY (D-7 / F-7, the load-bearing reason this rule keys on the VERB too):
// eclipse-powerwatch is the safe-shutdown guard. A stop/kill is DENIED HERE, at
// the rule itself (an explicit polkit.Result.NO) -- NOT merely a disabled UI
// button. A kiosk compromise, or a direct `systemctl stop eclipse-powerwatch`
// issued at the action path with the UI bypassed, is still refused. This is the
// defense-in-depth that mirrors US-407's action-path clear-gate re-check.
//
// Anything not on the allow-list returns no decision -> PolicyKit default deny.
//
// Install: deploy-pi.sh copies this to
//   /etc/polkit-1/rules.d/51-eclipse-service-control.rules
// (root-owned, 0644). PolicyKit auto-reloads on file change; no daemon-reload.
//
// Reference: US-403, Atlas A-7 (carousel/DTC design-gate signoff 2026-06-30),
//   design spec 2026-06-05 sec 4.6; I-036 / 50- polkit precedent.
// ============================================================================

polkit.addRule(function(action, subject) {
    if (action.id != "org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage-units" ||
        subject.user != "mcornelison") {
        return;  // not ours -> defer to other rules / PolicyKit default
    }

    var unit = action.lookup("unit");
    var verb = action.lookup("verb");

    // eclipse-powerwatch = the safe-shutdown guard: RESTART-ONLY. A stop/kill is
    // refused at the rule itself so the guard can never be removed from the UI
    // OR a bypassed action path (D-7 / F-7 defense-in-depth).
    if (unit == "eclipse-powerwatch.service") {
        if (verb == "restart") {
            return polkit.Result.YES;
        }
        return polkit.Result.NO;
    }

    // Data services + the dashboard kiosk: start / stop / restart.
    if (unit == "eclipse-obd.service" ||
        unit == "eclipse-sync.service" ||
        unit == "eclipse-dashboard.service") {
        if (verb == "start" || verb == "stop" || verb == "restart") {
            return polkit.Result.YES;
        }
    }

    // US-545 (A-18) -- NOT part of the kiosk mirror above.  eclipse-obd itself
    // runs as this user; when its connect path finds a de-bonded dongle it asks
    // systemd to run the bond self-heal (bond_self_heal.requestBondSelfHeal ->
    // `systemctl start --no-block`).  It cannot do the heal in-process because
    // the heal must STOP eclipse-obd first.
    //
    // START ONLY.  There is no kiosk button for this and none is intended --
    // the grant exists for the capture service, and polkit keys on the USER, so
    // it is reachable by any process of that user regardless.  That is not a new
    // exposure: `stop eclipse-obd.service` is ALREADY granted above, so anything
    // that could abuse this could already stop capture outright, more directly.
    // The self-heal is additionally self-limiting -- one re-pair per process,
    // and it restarts capture in a `finally` plus the unit's ExecStopPost.
    if (unit == "eclipse-bond-selfheal.service") {
        if (verb == "start") {
            return polkit.Result.YES;
        }
        return polkit.Result.NO;
    }

    // Any other unit, or a verb outside a unit's set -> no decision (default deny).
});
